the strategic use of shelves,

00:33:33.690 --> 00:33:37.320
drawers and partitions. In this
way the modern kitchen was

00:33:37.320 --> 00:33:40.770
linked to the office through a
faith in a cabinet logic that

00:33:40.770 --> 00:33:45.660
prioritized meticulously
organized interior storage to

00:33:45.660 --> 00:33:50.790
make things accessible. This was
captured in the Hoosier cabinet,

00:33:51.390 --> 00:33:55.530
six foot high and four feet
wide. Its large shelves and

00:33:55.530 --> 00:34:00.660
drawers held such items as pans,
kettles and nested mixing bowls

00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:04.260
all in specially designed
spaces. promotional materials

00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:09.900
claim that a Hoosier Cabinet had
400 articles all within an arm's

00:34:09.930 --> 00:34:14.190
reach. Manufacturers and writers
were keen to acknowledge the

00:34:14.190 --> 00:34:18.390
debt to the office vertical or
upright petitions called files

00:34:18.390 --> 00:34:21.510
were added shelves we still see
them sometimes today that allows

00:34:21.510 --> 00:34:24.900
plates and platters to be stored
on its edge quote, you can pick

00:34:24.900 --> 00:34:30.180
out with one hand just the dish
that you want. Ads to be

00:34:30.180 --> 00:34:33.510
expected were much more succinct
the business of getting meals.

00:34:33.690 --> 00:34:36.150
The kitchen needs to be
businesslike and in this ad, we

00:34:36.150 --> 00:34:39.660
can see a little cutout of an
office with a filing cabinet and

00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:44.400
with the vertical verticality of
the skyscraper as well. Now as

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:48.330
implied when announcing the move
from the office to the home,

00:34:48.330 --> 00:34:52.680
what I see important in these
changes in home storage is that

00:34:52.680 --> 00:34:56.010
they illustrate that storage
technologies require a certain

00:34:56.010 --> 00:34:59.310
form of labor performed by a
particular worker. Storage is

00:34:59.310 --> 00:35:02.670
not neutral. An encounter with
these technologies encourage

00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:06.330
women to understand their self
worth through productivity. As

00:35:06.330 --> 00:35:10.110
the interaction between hand and
object became the representation

00:35:10.290 --> 00:35:14.220
of efficient labor in the home,
these economic values became a

00:35:14.220 --> 00:35:18.600
way to express identity.
Addressed in these way, these

00:35:18.600 --> 00:35:21.840
women participated in a
reconfiguration of attitudes

00:35:21.840 --> 00:35:24.780
towards self and work
performance that helped make

00:35:24.780 --> 00:35:29.010
productivity common sense. And
adjustment that Mel Gregg argues

00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:34.560
gives productivity it's 20th
century history. I want to go

00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:37.650
further and link these changes
to information right to say

00:35:37.650 --> 00:35:41.280
although changes in domestic
storage did not address

00:35:41.310 --> 00:35:44.820
information as a formal
category, they do offer a

00:35:44.820 --> 00:35:49.770
suggestive example of how people
experience modern information

00:35:50.070 --> 00:35:54.060
via the materiality of storage
technologies. Right. So granular

00:35:54.060 --> 00:35:58.440
certainty, cabinet logic moved
to the house and brought with it

